import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'stale':('The phantom in his own boots',
  'After a teleport plus a blindness transition, a tracked monster entry can still point at the grid the player now occupies. No real monster can share the player\'s grid, but the melee chooser accepted distance zero as "adjacent", picked the phantom as the best target, and queued +5 - the center square, not a direction - which trips the unexpected-direction abort and stops the Borg. The correction requires distance exactly one: the phantom is no target, and nothing is queued.'),
 'control':('Control: a real adjacent kobold',
  'A genuinely adjacent monster one grid south is a valid target in both variants: the Borg attacks it with +2, and the complete log is byte-identical - the correction rejects only the impossible own-grid case.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/staletarget-322 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag in ('RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The phantom in his own boots</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native attack decisions</p><h1>The phantom in his own boots</h1><p>After a teleport plus a blindness transition, a tracked monster can still sit on the grid the player now occupies. The melee chooser accepted that stale entry as "adjacent" and attacked the player\'s own square - queuing the center key 5, which is not a direction, tripping the abort that stops the Borg.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>A genuinely adjacent monster is attacked identically in both variants: +2, byte for byte. The correction rejects only the impossible own-grid target.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior on a lit arena at depth 30, seed one thousand, a Broad Sword wielded, one observed awake Kobold. The stale situation moves the tracked entry onto the player\'s grid, exactly the post-teleport state the supplied run evidence recorded; the abort itself happens later, when the empty direction prompt is answered - this fixture measures the decision that produces it. The production attack chooser runs in acting mode and fills its own target list. No death claim; the recorded consequence is the stopped Borg.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/322">issue322</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let r=d.rating||'';let m=r.match(/acted=(\\d) keys=\\"([^\\"]*)\\"/);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=m?('Keys queued: '+(m[2]===''?'(none)':m[2])):'n/a';p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.outcome||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='stale'?'The original attacks his own grid: +5 queued, the center square - the abort that stops the Borg. The correction queues nothing: a stale entry is not a target.':'The real adjacent kobold is attacked identically: +2 in both variants, byte for byte.';}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
